From a2f8a9abda87bc6377e5cdc4ef01264a88822803 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:51:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: EXLR8 v0.7 experts on the mul1 codebook with E4M3
 rounding (mul1_e4m3 pieces)

kindlingai's EXLR8 release v0.7 (https://huggingface.co/kindlingai/glm-5.3-exlr8-k2-k3-k4, format https://github.com/kindlingai/exlr8)
re-encodes every routed and shared expert in the mul1 codebook, with every value rounded to E4M3 as in the earlier release's mcg
codebook. Patch 0205 read the earlier release through the mcg_e4m3 decode; this patch adds the mul1 one.

Kernel: exl3_decode.cuh gains CB_MUL1_E4M3 (build define TF_EXL3_MUL1_E4M3, set in the existing e4m3 expert and linear images):
the mul1 hash and single-rounded fp16 multiply-add as before, then the fp16 pair is rounded to E4M3 and back (round to nearest even,
saturating finite; the hardware cvt on sm_89 and up, an integer emulation proved exhaustively on older targets). mcg decoding and
images without the define are unchanged. zig/tests/exl3_mul1_e4m3_check.cu decodes all 65,536 states in both slots and compares
bit for bit with a host reference following kindlingai's reference loader (value rounded once to fp16, then to E4M3): 0 of 262,144
differ; the unrounded decode differs on 262,126 of 262,144 (the control).

Loader: the converter's rank pieces mark the codebook with a mul1_e4m3 tensor (0x83DCD12D) where 0205's pieces carry mcg_e4m3;
cuda_exl3.zig, config.zig, cuda_x8.zig, cuda_weights.zig and cuda_ranks.zig accept it (e4m3 set, Layer.codebook = mul1), refuse a layer
that mixes the two codebooks, and put the codebook in the rank agreement. Prompt expert kernels stay mcg-only, so mul1 layers prompt
through the grouped kernels (the host gate refuses them in exl3_prompt.zig). Host tests: test-glm-exl3-host 24/24.

Grouping of prompt picks past 64 KiB: tf_exl3_group staged rows * slots * 4 B of picks in shared memory, 128 KiB for a 4,096-row chunk at 8
slots, which fails to launch on GB10 (CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE, 64 KiB opted in). mcg layers prompt through the prompt kernels, so only
mul1 layers (which prompt through the grouped path) reached it: an 8,192-token prompt took the server down. The kernel now reads the picks
from global memory when they do not fit (GroupArgs.use_global, set by Experts.group); the same grouping, the same words.
